CAT = "txadjMarine"; SEG = "MAR"
Q = [
("Cargo is thrown overboard to save a ship in a storm. Under general average, the loss is:",
 "Shared by all interests saved", ["Borne by its owner alone", "Paid by the shipowner alone", "Excluded as an intentional act"],
 "General average spreads a voluntary sacrifice made to save the voyage among the ship, cargo and freight interests in proportion to their values."),
("Seawater ruins one shipper's goods in the hold, and no sacrifice was made for the voyage. This partial loss is:",
 "Particular average", ["General average", "A total loss", "A sue and labor charge"],
 "Particular average is a partial loss that falls only on the owner of the damaged property. General average needs a voluntary sacrifice for the common safety."),
("The ocean marine clause that covers a shipowner's liability for colliding with another vessel is the:",
 "Running down clause", ["Sue and labor clause", "Warehouse to warehouse", "Inchmaree clause"],
 "The running down (collision) clause covers the owner's liability for damage to another vessel and its cargo caused by a collision."),
("Protection and indemnity coverage pays a shipowner's liability for:",
 "Injuries to crew members", ["Damage to its own hull", "Freight income it loses", "Repairs from normal wear"],
 "P&I is the ocean marine liability coverage: injury to crew and others, damage to piers and other property, and similar legal liabilities. Hull insurance covers the vessel itself."),
("An HVAC contractor wants coverage for units it is installing at a customer's building until the job is accepted. It should buy:",
 "An installation floater", ["A bailee's customers policy", "A contractors equipment floater", "A garagekeepers policy"],
 "An installation floater covers materials and equipment being installed, while in transit, at the site and until the installation is accepted. An equipment floater covers the contractor's tools."),
("A personal articles floater on fine art usually covers the scheduled items:",
 "Worldwide, on open perils", ["Only at home, named perils", "In the US only, fire only", "Only while in transit"],
 "Personal and commercial floaters follow the property: scheduled items are typically covered anywhere in the world on an open perils basis."),
("After a fire, a city orders the undamaged half of an old building torn down. Ordinance or law Coverage A pays for:",
 "The value of the undamaged part", ["The cost of the demolition", "The higher cost to rebuild to code", "Rent lost during repairs"],
 "Coverage A pays the loss in value of the undamaged portion. Coverage B pays demolition cost, and Coverage C pays the increased cost of construction to meet code."),
("A law firm's client files are destroyed in a fire. The coverage that pays to research and re-create them is:",
 "Valuable papers and records", ["Accounts receivable", "Employee dishonesty", "Garagekeepers"],
 "Valuable papers and records coverage pays the cost to research, replace or restore lost information on documents. Accounts receivable pays sums the insured cannot collect."),
("A repair shop's coverage for damage to customers' cars left in its care is:",
 "Garagekeepers", ["Garage liability", "Business auto", "Motor truck cargo"],
 "Garagekeepers covers damage to customers' autos in the insured's care, custody or control. Garage liability covers injury and damage from the garage's operations."),
("An insured lets the underlying auto policy lapse and then causes a serious crash. The umbrella policy pays:",
 "As if the underlying were in force", ["From the first dollar of the loss", "Up to the underlying limit", "Half the loss, pro rata"],
 "If required underlying insurance is not maintained, the umbrella pays only what it would have paid had that insurance been in force. The insured bears the gap."),
("Boatowner and yacht policies usually limit where the vessel is covered through a:",
 "Navigation warranty", ["Coinsurance clause", "Running down clause", "Waiver of subrogation"],
 "A navigation warranty restricts the waters and sometimes the seasons in which the vessel may be used. A loss outside them is not covered unless the insurer agreed."),
("An adjusting firm is sued because its adjuster missed a deadline that cost a client money. The coverage that responds is:",
 "Errors and omissions", ["A fidelity bond", "Commercial crime", "General liability"],
 "Errors and omissions (professional liability) covers claims from negligent acts, errors or omissions in professional services. General liability excludes professional services."),
]
